{"content":[{"c":["HORMAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Town near Beersheba in the Negev and on the border of the tribes of Judah and Simeon. Originally a Canaanite settlement, it became Judah’s according to ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.30","r":"Josh.15.30","rawR":"Josh.15.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.30","value":"Josh.15.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Joshua 15:30"}," and then Simeon’s according to ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.4,9","r":"Josh.19.4,9","rawR":"Josh.19.4,9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.4,9","value":"Josh.19.4,9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Joshua 19:4, 9"},". Judah dominated it again by the time of the early monarchy (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.30.30","r":"1Sam.30.30","rawR":"1Sam.30.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.30.30","value":"1Sam.30.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 30:30"},"). The change of the Canaanite name Zephath to Hormah when the Hebrews first conquered it is noted in ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.1.17","r":"Judg.1.17","rawR":"Judg.1.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.1.17","value":"Judg.1.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Judges 1:17"},". Hormah took David’s side during his running feud with King Saul and David rewarded the town by sending it some of the spoils of Ziklag (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.30.1-31","r":"1Sam.30.1-31","rawR":"1Sam.30.1-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.30.1-31","value":"1Sam.30.1-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 30"},"). ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.30","r":"Josh.15.30","rawR":"Josh.15.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.30","value":"Josh.15.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Joshua 15:30"}," describes it as being in the south near Kesil and Ziklag, but its precise location remains unknown. From the reference in ",{"href":"?bref=Num.14.45","r":"Num.14.45","rawR":"Num.14.45","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.14.45","value":"Num.14.45"}],"t":"ref","v":"Numbers 14:45"},", it could well be south of Kadesh-barnea, where the Israelites spent much of the wilderness period."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Hormah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Joshua 15:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.30","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.30","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.30"},{"anchorText":"Joshua 19:4, 9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.4,9","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.4,9","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.4,9"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 30:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.30.30","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.30.30","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.30.30"},{"anchorText":"Judges 1:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.1.17","rawQueryValue":"Judg.1.17","sourceRefExact":"Judg.1.17"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.30.1-31","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.30.1-31","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.30.1-31"},{"anchorText":"Joshua 15:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.30","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.30","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.30"},{"anchorText":"Numbers 14:45","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.14.45","rawQueryValue":"Num.14.45","sourceRefExact":"Num.14.45"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"110e0bbd922472a374e1489b1a06361cb8c8c7758070dd848d723a58896bfc57","sourceItemName":"Hormah","sourceItemOrder":352,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Hormah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Hormah","title":"Hormah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}